              "text": "2mm thickness, 0.75mm distal taper thickness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Sits medial to Lister’s Tubercle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Distal K-Wire holes allow for additional small fragment fixation using paper-clip technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Volar Rim Plate",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423223/images/1dc37862-0e99-4db3-8e1e-2306f1478afe_screenshot_2025-03-27_at_9.18.57_am.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "SOMA designed",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "1.6mm thickness, 1.0mm distal taper thickness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "The vertical K-wire slots allow for distal or proximal adjustment and the horizontal K-wire slots allow for lateral or medial adjustment of the plate",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Sits on volar lip at the lunate facet",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Hooks to grab small distal fragments, which cannot be fixed with screws",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "K-wire holes can be used for placing sutures in the volar capsule",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Wrist Spanning Plate",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423223/images/fe4b1d96-2837-409a-af45-1c8e27a6a524_screenshot_2025-03-27_at_9.19.23_am_copy.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "SOMA designed",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "3mm thickness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Offered in 2 lengths",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Clustered pairs of holes are designed to align with dorsal distal radius and bones of the carpus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Tapered ends allow for easy plate sliding through ETC",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Specialized Instrumentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Plate Holding Reduction Clamp**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423257/images/f8a76f4a-4003-4288-9b2b-021e91e9d8c1_screenshot_2025-04-11_at_9.21.19_am.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed to assist with fracture reduction and plate retention",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "K-wire slots designed to aid with plate placement and distal K-wire fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Aiming Block**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423257/images/a4121b20-55f7-404f-9892-adb94b9785b0_screenshot_2025-04-11_at_9.21.25_am.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Comes pre-assembled with a set screw that attaches to plate through the distal threaded window hole",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Allows for drilling neutral axis of pre-angulated holes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Threaded Drill Tower**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423257/images/8ec89880-2ee7-4d49-86a3-6a5e03bfe965_screenshot_2025-04-11_at_9.21.31_am.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Fixed angle drill guide for all 2.4mm and 2.7mm screws",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Acts as a joystick to aid in plate positioning",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The VariAx 2 Distal Radius System is indicated for the treatment of:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Non-unions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Malunions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Deformities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approach",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Volar Plate/ Extended Volar Plate",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "An incision is made approximately 5 – 8cm long just radial to the FCR tendon.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "DR Dorsal Plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Longitudinal incision is made just ulnar to Lister’s tubercle at the distal radius region",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Lateral DR Plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "An incision is made along the radial column",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Dorsal Medial DR Plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "When plate is being used in conjunction with the lateral plate, incision is made between the 4th and 5th extensor compartments",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Dorsal Lateral DR Plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Longitudinal incision is made just ulnar to Lister’s tubercle at the distal radius region",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Volar Rim DR Plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Incision is made through a standard volar Henry approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Alternatively, a direct medial approach may provide superior exposure",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "For the direct medial approach, an extended carpal tunnel approach can be used distally and incorporated proximally to form an interval between the flexor tendons and the ulnar neurovascular bundle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Placement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Volar Plate/ Extended Volar Plate",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The plate should be placed slightly proximal to the distal edge of the radius to support the volar articular fracture fragment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "DR Dorsal Plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The plate should be placed slightly proximal the distal edge of the distal radius to avoid inserting screws/pegs into the joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Lateral DR Plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The brachioradialis can be elevated or the the plate can be placed directly on the brachiaradialis insertion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Dorsal Medial DR Plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The plate is slipped over the K-wire and placed along the dorsal ulnar corner",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Dorsal Lateral DR Plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The plate is slipped over the K-wire and placed along the dorsal radial corner",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Volar Rim DR Plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The plate is slipped over the K-wire and placed above volar capsule on the volar ulnar corner",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technical specifications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Locking screws are laser marked with a ‘dot’ and ‘ring’ marking on the screw head to differentiate them from non-locking screws",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Locking and Non-Locking screws can be used in any round hole",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Allows for ±15 degrees of angulation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The 2.0mm drill guide for T8 Screws facilitates drilling a 2.0mm pilot hole for a 2.4 or 2.7mm T8 screw or a 2.0mm peg centrically for locking or non-locking screws",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Screws",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "2.7mm Screws T8 Interface",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423223/images/9d7b4788-9c58-4be2-9522-5178c77c8528_screenshot_2025-03-27_at_10.22.22_am.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Locking & non-locking",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Purple",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "2.4mm Screws and 2.0mm Pegs T8 Interface",
          "table": null,
